The diameter of a wire XY varies linearly with distance along the wire as shown in Fig. 7.1.
{{figure:figure_7_1}}
There is a current $I$ in the wire. At end X of the wire, the diameter is $d$ and the average drift speed of the free electrons is $v_{x}$. At end Y of the wire, the diameter is $\frac{d}{2}$.
On Fig. 7.2, sketch a graph to show the variation of the average drift speed with position along the wire between X and Y.
{{figure:figure_7_2}}

